/*--------------------------------*- Choupo -*--------------------------------*\
  species/Glyc.dat -- ONE model species, ONE typed file: the fully dissociated form of glycolic acid.
  Made by bin/curate/species_c373.py from data/curation/batches/species_c373/*.tsv, which holds every
  reading (source, table, page, whether read from a page image).  Standard state: ideal solution at
  1 mol/kg, 298.15 K, H+ = 0.
  The formation values are DERIVED from printed numbers; the arithmetic, tables and pages are in the
  source line below and in formation.tsv.
\*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
recordType modelSpecies;
schemaVersion 1;

name    Glyc;
formula     "C2H3O3-";
charge  -1;
MW { value 75.043; unit g/mol;}
aqueousThermo
{
source "hfAq [kJ/mol] -647.60: HGlyc -648.06 plus dH_ion +0.46 (MILL90 Table 6) -- Shock, Organic acids in hydrothermal solutions: standard molal thermodynamic properties of carboxylic acids, and estimates of dissociation constants at high temperatures and pressures, Am. J. Sci. 295 (1995) 496-580, Table 10, p. 544 (acid) and steps.tsv (dH_ion) (read from a page image), one scale with the evaluated step: the paper's own glycolate DfH is -154700 cal = -647.28 kJ/mol, calculated by it from DfG and S (footnote r), 0.32 kJ/mol from this ## sAq [J/mol/K] 108.33: HGlyc 180.33 plus dS_ion -72.0 (MILL90 Table 6) -- Shock, Organic acids in hydrothermal solutions: standard molal thermodynamic properties of carboxylic acids, and estimates of dissociation constants at high temperatures and pressures, Am. J. Sci. 295 (1995) 496-580, Table 10, p. 544 (acid) and steps.tsv (dS_ion) (read from a page image), the paper prints 26.2 cal/mol/K = 109.62 J/mol/K (estimated, footnote h, eq 40), the value entered follows the acid's estimate and the printed dissociation entropy so that the family holds the Gibbs identity";
hfAq { value -647600; unit J/mol;}
sAq  { value 108.33; unit J/mol/K;}
provenance
{
    sAq
    {
        origin  estimated;
        method  "Shock (1995): acid S ESTIMATED (Table 10 footnote g) plus Miller & Smith-Magowan's printed dissociation entropy";
    }
}
}
